fn word_under_cursor(cmd_line: &str, cursor_x: usize) -> Option<String> {
    // cursor_x is char index (0..len, where len means after last char, e.g., end)
    // If line empty, None. If cursor on word char (non-space), return that word (space-delimited). If on space or beyond end, return previous word (to left). If no previous word (e.g., leading spaces, empty before), None? Actually for empty command, F5 does nothing (no menu). For command with only spaces? Probably None.
